              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Is GFC better than PRP?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Not necessarily. The two are related, and neither is proven better for everyone. Your diagnosis should guide the choice."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Is GFC treatment surgical?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "No. It involves a blood draw and scalp injections, with no cuts or stitches."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Does GFC work for baldness?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "It is meant for thinning hair where follicles are still active. It is not intended for completely bald areas."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Are there side effects?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Mild redness, soreness or swelling can occur and usually settles quickly. Rarely, infection is possible. Share your medical history with the doctor before treatment."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "How soon will I see a difference?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Hair grows slowly. Any change is usually assessed over several months, and results differ from person to person."
              }
            }
